Wayland: tag SHM video frames on the WebRender compositor path as Texture2D

With the WebRender native compositor on Wayland (Firefox enables it together
with HDR), BufferTextureHost hands software-decoded/SHM video frames to
WebRender through RenderWaylandTextureHost. Those frames are uploaded into
ordinary GL_TEXTURE_2D textures (SHMBufSurface::UploadTexture), but the image
was tagged ImageBufferKind::TextureRect. WebRender only builds TEXTURE_RECT
shader variants on desktop GL; on GLES (the default on GTK/aarch64,
gfx.egl.prefer-gles) the first such frame drawn through the quad path (any
clipped or rounded video, e.g. a YouTube player) panics with
"bug: ps_quad_textured TEXTURE_RECT variant not loaded" and takes the parent
process down.

Backport of the BufferTextureHost::PushResourceUpdates hunk of upstream
Bug 2084900 (e1da14d64fab, "Use RenderLinuxTextureHost for Wayland compositor
and make direct composition optional"), which tags these textures as
Texture2D. The rest of that change (RenderLinuxTextureHost refactor) is not
needed for the fix.

--- a/gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp
+++ b/gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp
@@ -560,9 +560,12 @@
       aResources.GetCapabilities().mBackendType, GetSize());
   bool useNativeTexture =
       (policy == REQUIRE) || (policy != FORBID && UseExternalTextures());
-  auto imageType = useNativeTexture ? wr::ExternalImageType::TextureHandle(
-                                          wr::ImageBufferKind::TextureRect)
-                                    : wr::ExternalImageType::Buffer();
+  // External textures are used on Wayland where texture 2D is used.
+  auto textureType = UseExternalTextures() ? wr::ImageBufferKind::Texture2D
+                                           : wr::ImageBufferKind::TextureRect;
+  auto imageType = useNativeTexture
+                       ? wr::ExternalImageType::TextureHandle(textureType)
+                       : wr::ExternalImageType::Buffer();
 
   if (!IsYCbCr()) {
     if (aImageKeys.length() != 1) {
